nd": "variable", "doc": "<p>Token id, unique within <code>context</code> (e.g. 't1', 't2', ...).</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.CitableToken.value": {"fullname": "aat.CitableToken.value", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "CitableToken.value", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>The token's own string value (its surface text).</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.CitedPassage": {"fullname": "aat.CitedPassage", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "CitedPassage", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>One citable passage of text: a reference identifying its context\n(aat-model.md's example is a CTS URN, but any stable identifier a\ncaller chooses works -- nothing here assumes CTS specifically) paired\nwith the passage's own raw text.</p>\n", "bases": "pydantic.main.BaseModel"}, "aat.CitedPassage.context": {"fullname": "aat.CitedPassage.context", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "CitedPassage.context", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Reference identifying this passage's context, e.g. a CTS URN.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.CitedPassage.text": {"fullname": "aat.CitedPassage.text", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "CitedPassage.text", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>This passage's raw text, exactly as written.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.AATGraph": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>A full AAT graph for one or more citable passages: an ordered list\nof AATNode. Node order is not semantically significant -- the\nconvenience accessors below don't depend on it -- but callers that\nbuilt the graph from a specific passage will typically find document\norder convenient for display.</p>\n", "bases": "pydantic.main.BaseModel"}, "aat.AATGraph.nodes": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.nodes", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.nodes", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p></p>\n", "annotation": ": List[aat.core.graph.AATNode]", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.AATGraph.by_id": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.by_id", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.by_id", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>The node with this (context, id), or None. <code>id</code> alone isn't a\nreliable key across contexts (CitableToken/AATNode ids are only\nunique <em>within</em> one context -- see CitableToken's docstring), so\nboth are required here.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"nb\">id</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.AATGraph.actions": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.actions", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.actions", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every action node, in list order.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.AATGraph.agents": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.agents", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.agents", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every agent node, in list order.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.AATGraph.targets": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.targets", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.targets", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every target node, in list order.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.AATGraph.agents_for": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.agents_for", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.agents_for", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every agent node whose related_node points at <code>action</code>'s id,\nwithin the same context.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.AATGraph.targets_for": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.targets_for", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.targets_for", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every target node whose related_node points at <code>action</code>'s id,\nwithin the same context.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.AATGraph.governing_action": {"fullname": "aat.AATGraph.governing_action", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATGraph.governing_action", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>For a dependent action node, the action node it's subordinate\nto; None if <code>action</code> is independent (related_node is None) or if\nrelated_node doesn't resolve to any node in this graph.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.AATNode": {"fullname": "aat.AATNode", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATNode", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>One node in an AAT graph.</p>\n\n<p><code>context</code> and <code>id</code> identify the token this node is built from -- for a\nsingle-token action, an agent, or a target, <code>id</code> is just that token's\nown id. For a <em>compound</em> action (aat-model.md's \"Actions\" section --\ne.g. \"was eating\"), <code>id</code> is instead the id of the <em>principal verb</em>\ntoken within the compound (e.g. the token for \"eating\"), and <code>value</code>\nis the space-joined text of every component token in surface order\n(e.g. \"was eating\"), not just the principal verb's own text.</p>\n\n<p><code>related_node</code> is:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>None</code>, for an <em>independent</em> action node (aat-model.md's\n\"Actions\" section);</li>\n<li>another action node's <code>id</code>, for a <em>dependent</em> action node (the id\nof the governing action it depends on);</li>\n<li>another action node's <code>id</code>, for an agent or target node (the id\nof the action it's the agent/target of) -- agent and target nodes\nalways have a related_node; only an action node's related_node\ncan be <code>None</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n", "bases": "pydantic.main.BaseModel"}, "aat.AATNode.context": {"fullname": "aat.AATNode.context", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATNode.context", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Context reference this node belongs to.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.AATNode.id": {"fullname": "aat.AATNode.id", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATNode.id", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Token id this node is built from -- the principal verb's id for a compound action, otherwise the single underlying token's id.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.AATNode.value": {"fullname": "aat.AATNode.value", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATNode.value", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>This node's string value -- a single token's own text, or, for a compound action, every component token's text joined by spaces in surface order.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.AATNode.role": {"fullname": "aat.AATNode.role", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATNode.role", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>'agent', 'action', or 'target'.</p>\n", "annotation": ": Literal[&#x27;agent&#x27;, &#x27;action&#x27;, &#x27;target&#x27;]", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.AATNode.related_node": {"fullname": "aat.AATNode.related_node", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "AATNode.related_node", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>For an action node: the id of the governing action node, if this action is dependent/subordinate; None if independent. For an agent or target node: the id of the action node it relates to (always set).</p>\n", "annotation": ": str | None", "default_value": "None"}, "aat.Role": {"fullname": "aat.Role", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "Role", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p></p>\n", "default_value": "typing.Literal[&#x27;agent&#x27;, &#x27;action&#x27;, &#x27;target&#x27;]"}, "aat.ROLES": {"fullname": "aat.ROLES", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "ROLES", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p></p>\n", "default_value": "(&#x27;agent&#x27;, &#x27;action&#x27;, &#x27;target&#x27;)"}, "aat.validate": {"fullname": "aat.validate", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "validate", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Return a list of human-readable problem descriptions found in\n<code>graph</code>, given the <code>tokens</code> it was built from. An empty list means no\nreferential problems were found (not that the analysis is correct).</p>\n\n<h6 id=\"checks\">Checks:</h6>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <ul>\n  <li>every node's (context, id) matches a real token in <code>tokens</code>;</li>\n  <li>every node's <code>value</code> is non-empty;</li>\n  <li>an action node's <code>related_node</code>, if set, resolves to another\n  action node's id in the same context;</li>\n  <li>an agent or target node's <code>related_node</code> is set (not None) and\n  resolves to an action node's id in the same context.</li>\n  </ul>\n</blockquote>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitableToken</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.serialize_nodes": {"fullname": "aat.serialize_nodes", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "serialize_nodes", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Render <code>nodes</code> as one '#!aatnodes' block, pipe-delimited, and\nreturn it as a string. Does not check for '|' inside any field's own\nvalue -- there is no escaping mechanism, so avoid the delimiter\ncharacter in <code>value</code> if you plan to round-trip through this format.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.write_nodes": {"fullname": "aat.write_nodes", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "write_nodes", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write serialize_nodes(nodes) to <code>path</code>.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.read_nodes": {"fullname": "aat.read_nodes", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "read_nodes", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Read every '#!aatnodes' block in <code>path</code> and return their rows,\nconcatenated in file order, as a list of AATNode -- other block\ntypes in the same file (e.g. a '#!passages' block) are ignored, see\n_read_blocks().</p>\n\n<p>Raises ValueError (via _read_blocks()) for a malformed file -- see\nthat function's own docstring for the exact cases. Also raises\nValueError (not returning an empty list) if the file has no\n'#!aatnodes' block at all, so a caller can't mistake \"wrong file\" for\n\"file with zero nodes\".</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.read_graph": {"fullname": "aat.read_graph", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "read_graph", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Convenience wrapper: read_nodes(path) wrapped as an AATGraph.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.serialize_passages": {"fullname": "aat.serialize_passages", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "serialize_passages", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Render <code>passages</code> as one '#!passages' block, pipe-delimited, and\nreturn it as a string. Same no-escaping caveat as serialize_nodes():\navoid '|' in <code>text</code> if you plan to round-trip through this format.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.write_passages": {"fullname": "aat.write_passages", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "write_passages", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write serialize_passages(passages) to <code>path</code>.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.read_passages": {"fullname": "aat.read_passages", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "read_passages", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Read every '#!passages' block in <code>path</code> and return their rows,\nconcatenated in file order, as a list of CitedPassage -- other block\ntypes in the same file (e.g. a '#!aatnodes' block) are ignored, see\n_read_blocks().</p>\n\n<p>Raises ValueError (via _read_blocks()) for a malformed file. Also\nraises ValueError if the file has no '#!passages' block at all, same\nreasoning as read_nodes().</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.serialize_analysis": {"fullname": "aat.serialize_analysis", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "serialize_analysis", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Render a complete, re-displayable analysis as one string: a\n'#!passages' block (so aat.english.tokenize() can deterministically\nrebuild tokens later with no LM access needed at all) followed by a\n'#!aatnodes' block (the AAT graph an earlier, LM-dependent analysis\nstep produced). write_analysis() is a thin wrapper that writes this\nsame string to a file; call this directly instead when the text\nitself is what's wanted -- e.g. to hand to a UI that writes the file\nsomewhere else (a chosen directory, a download, ...), or to embed\nthe analysis in something larger without touching disk here at all.\nread_analysis() is the matching reader for a file written either\nway -- see that function's own docstring for the intended round\ntrip.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.write_analysis": {"fullname": "aat.write_analysis", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "write_analysis", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write serialize_analysis(passages, graph) to <code>path</code>. See that\nfunction's own docstring for exactly what gets written, and\nread_analysis() for the matching reader.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.read_analysis": {"fullname": "aat.read_analysis", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "read_analysis", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Read a file written by write_analysis(): both its '#!passages'\nblock (as a list of CitedPassage) and its '#!aatnodes' block (as an\nAATGraph). Raises ValueError if either block is missing -- see\nread_passages()/read_nodes().</p>\n\n<p>A caller that only has <code>path</code> and needs tokens to pair back up with\nthe returned graph (e.g. to highlight them with\naat.english.html.tokens_to_html()) re-tokenizes each returned\npassage with aat.english.tokenize() -- deterministic and LM-free, so\nthis whole round trip needs no LM access at any point.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.graph_to_mermaid": {"fullname": "aat.graph_to_mermaid", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "graph_to_mermaid", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Build a Mermaid <code>graph</code> diagram from an AATGraph.</p>\n\n<p><code>orientation</code> is Mermaid's own flowchart direction code -- <code>BT</code>\n(bottom-to-top, the default here), <code>TB</code>/<code>TD</code> (top-down -- synonyms),\n<code>LR</code>, or <code>RL</code> -- used verbatim (uppercased) in the diagram's opening\nline (<code>graph BT</code>, etc.). Matched case-insensitively against\n<code>_VALID_ORIENTATIONS</code>; anything else raises <code>ValueError</code> naming the\nvalid options, rather than silently producing invalid Mermaid syntax.\nSee <a href=\"https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/flowchart.html#direction\">https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/flowchart.html#direction</a>.</p>\n\n<p><code>color_by_action</code> (default True) -- see this module's own docstring.\nPass False for a plain, uncolored diagram.</p>\n\n<p>Returns (diagram_text, warnings). A node whose <code>related_node</code> doesn't\nresolve to any node actually present in <code>graph</code> (same context) is\nstill drawn, but its edge is skipped and reported as a warning --\nnormally a sign <code>graph</code> failed aat.core.validate.validate() upstream,\nworth checking there first. If <code>color_by_action</code> is True and the graph\nhas more distinct actions than the palette has colors (currently 8),\none warning notes that colors repeat.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">orientation</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s1\">'BT'</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">color_by_action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">bool</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">True</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.save_mermaid": {"fullname": "aat.save_mermaid", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "save_mermaid", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write the diagram to <code>path</code> (e.g. 'analysis.mmd') and return any\nwarnings from graph_to_mermaid(). <code>orientation</code> is validated the same\nway -- see graph_to_mermaid()'s own docstring.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">orientation</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s1\">'BT'</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">color_by_action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">bool</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">True</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.assign_action_colors": {"fullname": "aat.assign_action_colors", "modulename": "aat", "qualname": "assign_action_colors", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Return (color_of_node, warnings).</p>\n\n<p><code>color_of_node</code> maps every node's (context, id) to a (fill, stroke,\ntext) hex triple, for every node that clusters with some action: an\naction node itself (dependent or not -- see this module's own\ndocstring), or an agent/target node whose <code>related_node</code> resolves to\nan action node in the same context. A node with no resolvable cluster\n(e.g. an agent/target with a broken related_node -- shouldn't happen\nin a graph that's passed aat.core.validate.validate()) is simply\nabsent from the mapping.</p>\n\n<p>Colors are assigned to actions in the order they first appear in\n<code>graph.nodes</code>, cycling through the palette (currently 8 colors) if\nthere are more distinct actions than that -- in which case two\ndistinct actions (and their own agent/target nodes) end up sharing the\nidentical color. <code>warnings</code> has one entry naming this when it happens;\notherwise it's empty.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Dict</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]],</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core": {"fullname": "aat.core", "modulename": "aat.core", "kind": "module", "doc": "<p>aat.core: the Agent-Action-Target model itself (aat-model.md), with no\ndependency on any particular language or on dspy.</p>\n\n<p>Everything in this subpackage represents, validates, serializes, or\nrenders an AAT graph; nothing here knows how to <em>produce</em> one from real\ntext -- that's aat.english's job (or, eventually, another language-\nspecific sibling subpackage). Keeping this boundary means aat.core can be\nimported and reused on its own by any downstream project that just wants\nthe data model, the file format, and the Mermaid renderer, without\npulling in dspy at all.</p>\n"}, "aat.core.CitableToken": {"fullname": "aat.core.CitableToken", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "CitableToken", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>One token belonging to a citable passage.</p>\n\n<p><code>id</code> is unique <em>within</em> <code>context</code>, not globally -- aat-model.md's own\nworked example uses a per-context sequence like 't1', 't2', ...,\nstarting over for each new context. A caller working across multiple\ncontexts should treat (context, id) as the real compound key, not id\nalone -- see AATGraph.by_id().</p>\n", "bases": "pydantic.main.BaseModel"}, "aat.core.CitableToken.context": {"fullname": "aat.core.CitableToken.context", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "CitableToken.context", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Context reference this token belongs to, matching its source CitedPassage.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.CitableToken.id": {"fullname": "aat.core.CitableToken.id", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "CitableToken.id", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Token id, unique within <code>context</code> (e.g. 't1', 't2', ...).</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.CitableToken.value": {"fullname": "aat.core.CitableToken.value", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "CitableToken.value", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>The token's own string value (its surface text).</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.CitedPassage": {"fullname": "aat.core.CitedPassage", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "CitedPassage", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>One citable passage of text: a reference identifying its context\n(aat-model.md's example is a CTS URN, but any stable identifier a\ncaller chooses works -- nothing here assumes CTS specifically) paired\nwith the passage's own raw text.</p>\n", "bases": "pydantic.main.BaseModel"}, "aat.core.CitedPassage.context": {"fullname": "aat.core.CitedPassage.context", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "CitedPassage.context", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Reference identifying this passage's context, e.g. a CTS URN.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.CitedPassage.text": {"fullname": "aat.core.CitedPassage.text", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "CitedPassage.text", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>This passage's raw text, exactly as written.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.AATGraph": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>A full AAT graph for one or more citable passages: an ordered list\nof AATNode. Node order is not semantically significant -- the\nconvenience accessors below don't depend on it -- but callers that\nbuilt the graph from a specific passage will typically find document\norder convenient for display.</p>\n", "bases": "pydantic.main.BaseModel"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.nodes": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.nodes", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.nodes", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p></p>\n", "annotation": ": List[aat.core.graph.AATNode]", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.by_id": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.by_id", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.by_id", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>The node with this (context, id), or None. <code>id</code> alone isn't a\nreliable key across contexts (CitableToken/AATNode ids are only\nunique <em>within</em> one context -- see CitableToken's docstring), so\nboth are required here.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"nb\">id</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.actions": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.actions", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.actions", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every action node, in list order.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.agents": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.agents", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.agents", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every agent node, in list order.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.targets": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.targets", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.targets", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every target node, in list order.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.agents_for": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.agents_for", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.agents_for", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every agent node whose related_node points at <code>action</code>'s id,\nwithin the same context.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.targets_for": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.targets_for", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.targets_for", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Every target node whose related_node points at <code>action</code>'s id,\nwithin the same context.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.AATGraph.governing_action": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATGraph.governing_action", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATGraph.governing_action", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>For a dependent action node, the action node it's subordinate\nto; None if <code>action</code> is independent (related_node is None) or if\nrelated_node doesn't resolve to any node in this graph.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"bp\">self</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.AATNode": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATNode", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATNode", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>One node in an AAT graph.</p>\n\n<p><code>context</code> and <code>id</code> identify the token this node is built from -- for a\nsingle-token action, an agent, or a target, <code>id</code> is just that token's\nown id. For a <em>compound</em> action (aat-model.md's \"Actions\" section --\ne.g. \"was eating\"), <code>id</code> is instead the id of the <em>principal verb</em>\ntoken within the compound (e.g. the token for \"eating\"), and <code>value</code>\nis the space-joined text of every component token in surface order\n(e.g. \"was eating\"), not just the principal verb's own text.</p>\n\n<p><code>related_node</code> is:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><code>None</code>, for an <em>independent</em> action node (aat-model.md's\n\"Actions\" section);</li>\n<li>another action node's <code>id</code>, for a <em>dependent</em> action node (the id\nof the governing action it depends on);</li>\n<li>another action node's <code>id</code>, for an agent or target node (the id\nof the action it's the agent/target of) -- agent and target nodes\nalways have a related_node; only an action node's related_node\ncan be <code>None</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n", "bases": "pydantic.main.BaseModel"}, "aat.core.AATNode.context": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATNode.context", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATNode.context", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Context reference this node belongs to.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.AATNode.id": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATNode.id", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATNode.id", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Token id this node is built from -- the principal verb's id for a compound action, otherwise the single underlying token's id.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.AATNode.value": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATNode.value", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATNode.value", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>This node's string value -- a single token's own text, or, for a compound action, every component token's text joined by spaces in surface order.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.AATNode.role": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATNode.role", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATNode.role", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>'agent', 'action', or 'target'.</p>\n", "annotation": ": Literal[&#x27;agent&#x27;, &#x27;action&#x27;, &#x27;target&#x27;]", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.core.AATNode.related_node": {"fullname": "aat.core.AATNode.related_node", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "AATNode.related_node", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>For an action node: the id of the governing action node, if this action is dependent/subordinate; None if independent. For an agent or target node: the id of the action node it relates to (always set).</p>\n", "annotation": ": str | None", "default_value": "None"}, "aat.core.Role": {"fullname": "aat.core.Role", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "Role", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p></p>\n", "default_value": "typing.Literal[&#x27;agent&#x27;, &#x27;action&#x27;, &#x27;target&#x27;]"}, "aat.core.ROLES": {"fullname": "aat.core.ROLES", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "ROLES", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p></p>\n", "default_value": "(&#x27;agent&#x27;, &#x27;action&#x27;, &#x27;target&#x27;)"}, "aat.core.validate": {"fullname": "aat.core.validate", "modulename": "aat.core.validate", "kind": "module", "doc": "<p>Referential validation for an AATGraph: does every node actually resolve\nto something real, given the token list it claims to be built from? This\nchecks referential integrity only -- never correctness of the underlying\nlinguistic analysis; see aat.english.pipeline / DEVELOPMENT.md for how the\nEnglish pipeline builds on top of this.</p>\n"}, "aat.core.serialize_nodes": {"fullname": "aat.core.serialize_nodes", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "serialize_nodes", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Render <code>nodes</code> as one '#!aatnodes' block, pipe-delimited, and\nreturn it as a string. Does not check for '|' inside any field's own\nvalue -- there is no escaping mechanism, so avoid the delimiter\ncharacter in <code>value</code> if you plan to round-trip through this format.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.write_nodes": {"fullname": "aat.core.write_nodes", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "write_nodes", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write serialize_nodes(nodes) to <code>path</code>.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">nodes</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.read_nodes": {"fullname": "aat.core.read_nodes", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "read_nodes", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Read every '#!aatnodes' block in <code>path</code> and return their rows,\nconcatenated in file order, as a list of AATNode -- other block\ntypes in the same file (e.g. a '#!passages' block) are ignored, see\n_read_blocks().</p>\n\n<p>Raises ValueError (via _read_blocks()) for a malformed file -- see\nthat function's own docstring for the exact cases. Also raises\nValueError (not returning an empty list) if the file has no\n'#!aatnodes' block at all, so a caller can't mistake \"wrong file\" for\n\"file with zero nodes\".</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATNode</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.read_graph": {"fullname": "aat.core.read_graph", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "read_graph", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Convenience wrapper: read_nodes(path) wrapped as an AATGraph.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.serialize_passages": {"fullname": "aat.core.serialize_passages", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "serialize_passages", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Render <code>passages</code> as one '#!passages' block, pipe-delimited, and\nreturn it as a string. Same no-escaping caveat as serialize_nodes():\navoid '|' in <code>text</code> if you plan to round-trip through this format.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.write_passages": {"fullname": "aat.core.write_passages", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "write_passages", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write serialize_passages(passages) to <code>path</code>.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>, </span><span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.read_passages": {"fullname": "aat.core.read_passages", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "read_passages", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Read every '#!passages' block in <code>path</code> and return their rows,\nconcatenated in file order, as a list of CitedPassage -- other block\ntypes in the same file (e.g. a '#!aatnodes' block) are ignored, see\n_read_blocks().</p>\n\n<p>Raises ValueError (via _read_blocks()) for a malformed file. Also\nraises ValueError if the file has no '#!passages' block at all, same\nreasoning as read_nodes().</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code condensed\">(<span class=\"param\"><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.serialize_analysis": {"fullname": "aat.core.serialize_analysis", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "serialize_analysis", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Render a complete, re-displayable analysis as one string: a\n'#!passages' block (so aat.english.tokenize() can deterministically\nrebuild tokens later with no LM access needed at all) followed by a\n'#!aatnodes' block (the AAT graph an earlier, LM-dependent analysis\nstep produced). write_analysis() is a thin wrapper that writes this\nsame string to a file; call this directly instead when the text\nitself is what's wanted -- e.g. to hand to a UI that writes the file\nsomewhere else (a chosen directory, a download, ...), or to embed\nthe analysis in something larger without touching disk here at all.\nread_analysis() is the matching reader for a file written either\nway -- see that function's own docstring for the intended round\ntrip.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.write_analysis": {"fullname": "aat.core.write_analysis", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "write_analysis", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write serialize_analysis(passages, graph) to <code>path</code>. See that\nfunction's own docstring for exactly what gets written, and\nread_analysis() for the matching reader.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.read_analysis": {"fullname": "aat.core.read_analysis", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "read_analysis", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Read a file written by write_analysis(): both its '#!passages'\nblock (as a list of CitedPassage) and its '#!aatnodes' block (as an\nAATGraph). Raises ValueError if either block is missing -- see\nread_passages()/read_nodes().</p>\n\n<p>A caller that only has <code>path</code> and needs tokens to pair back up with\nthe returned graph (e.g. to highlight them with\naat.english.html.tokens_to_html()) re-tokenizes each returned\npassage with aat.english.tokenize() -- deterministic and LM-free, so\nthis whole round trip needs no LM access at any point.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.graph_to_mermaid": {"fullname": "aat.core.graph_to_mermaid", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "graph_to_mermaid", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Build a Mermaid <code>graph</code> diagram from an AATGraph.</p>\n\n<p><code>orientation</code> is Mermaid's own flowchart direction code -- <code>BT</code>\n(bottom-to-top, the default here), <code>TB</code>/<code>TD</code> (top-down -- synonyms),\n<code>LR</code>, or <code>RL</code> -- used verbatim (uppercased) in the diagram's opening\nline (<code>graph BT</code>, etc.). Matched case-insensitively against\n<code>_VALID_ORIENTATIONS</code>; anything else raises <code>ValueError</code> naming the\nvalid options, rather than silently producing invalid Mermaid syntax.\nSee <a href=\"https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/flowchart.html#direction\">https://mermaid.js.org/syntax/flowchart.html#direction</a>.</p>\n\n<p><code>color_by_action</code> (default True) -- see this module's own docstring.\nPass False for a plain, uncolored diagram.</p>\n\n<p>Returns (diagram_text, warnings). A node whose <code>related_node</code> doesn't\nresolve to any node actually present in <code>graph</code> (same context) is\nstill drawn, but its edge is skipped and reported as a warning --\nnormally a sign <code>graph</code> failed aat.core.validate.validate() upstream,\nworth checking there first. If <code>color_by_action</code> is True and the graph\nhas more distinct actions than the palette has colors (currently 8),\none warning notes that colors repeat.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">orientation</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s1\">'BT'</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">color_by_action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">bool</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">True</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.save_mermaid": {"fullname": "aat.core.save_mermaid", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "save_mermaid", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Write the diagram to <code>path</code> (e.g. 'analysis.mmd') and return any\nwarnings from graph_to_mermaid(). <code>orientation</code> is validated the same\nway -- see graph_to_mermaid()'s own docstring.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">orientation</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s1\">'BT'</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">color_by_action</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">bool</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">True</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.assign_action_colors": {"fullname": "aat.core.assign_action_colors", "modulename": "aat.core", "qualname": "assign_action_colors", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Return (color_of_node, warnings).</p>\n\n<p><code>color_of_node</code> maps every node's (context, id) to a (fill, stroke,\ntext) hex triple, for every node that clusters with some action: an\naction node itself (dependent or not -- see this module's own\ndocstring), or an agent/target node whose <code>related_node</code> resolves to\nan action node in the same context. A node with no resolvable cluster\n(e.g. an agent/target with a broken related_node -- shouldn't happen\nin a graph that's passed aat.core.validate.validate()) is simply\nabsent from the mapping.</p>\n\n<p>Colors are assigned to actions in the order they first appear in\n<code>graph.nodes</code>, cycling through the palette (currently 8 colors) if\nthere are more distinct actions than that -- in which case two\ndistinct actions (and their own agent/target nodes) end up sharing the\nidentical color. <code>warnings</code> has one entry naming this when it happens;\notherwise it's empty.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Dict</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]],</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.core.validate.validate": {"fullname": "aat.core.validate.validate", "modulename": "aat.core.validate", "qualname": "validate", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Return a list of human-readable problem descriptions found in\n<code>graph</code>, given the <code>tokens</code> it was built from. An empty list means no\nreferential problems were found (not that the analysis is correct).</p>\n\n<h6 id=\"checks\">Checks:</h6>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <ul>\n  <li>every node's (context, id) matches a real token in <code>tokens</code>;</li>\n  <li>every node's <code>value</code> is non-empty;</li>\n  <li>an action node's <code>related_node</code>, if set, resolves to another\n  action node's id in the same context;</li>\n  <li>an agent or target node's <code>related_node</code> is set (not None) and\n  resolves to an action node's id in the same context.</li>\n  </ul>\n</blockquote>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitableToken</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.english": {"fullname": "aat.english", "modulename": "aat.english", "kind": "module", "doc": "<p>aat.english: applies the Agent-Action-Target model (aat.core, aat-model.md)\nto English text, using a DSPy program to do the actual semantic\nextraction.</p>\n\n<p>Needs the 'english' extra (dspy) -- <code>pip install aat[english]</code>, or (from\nGitHub) <code>pip install \"aat[english] @ git+https://github.com/neelsmith/aat.git\"</code>.\nNothing in aat.core imports this module or requires dspy; the dependency\nruns one way only, so a downstream project can depend on aat.core alone.</p>\n"}, "aat.english.tokenize": {"fullname": "aat.english.tokenize", "modulename": "aat.english.tokenize", "kind": "module", "doc": "<p>A deterministic tokenizer for English text: turns a CitedPassage into a\nlist of CitableToken, per aat-model.md's \"Context and tokens\" section\n(worked example: \"The dog ate my homework.\" tokenizes to \"The\", \"dog\",\n\"ate\", \"my\", \"homework\", \".\" -- six tokens, \"t1\" as the first token's id).</p>\n\n<p>This is deliberately mechanical, not semantic -- splitting words from\npunctuation is unambiguous enough in English to not need an LLM call at\nall (contrast a language like Latin, where enclitics can make tokenization\nitself genuinely ambiguous and worth handing to an LLM). The actual\nAgent-Action-Target role assignment -- the hard, semantic part -- is\ndspy_signatures.py's job, not this module's.</p>\n"}, "aat.english.AgentActionTarget": {"fullname": "aat.english.AgentActionTarget", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "AgentActionTarget", "kind": "class", "doc": "<p>Analyze an English passage according to the Agent-Action-Target\n(AAT) model documented in aat-model.md.</p>\n\n<p>Extract every <em>action</em> (verbal expression): a single token for a\nsimple verb (e.g. \"ate\"), or, for a compound verbal expression (e.g.\n\"was eating\", \"was being eaten\"), a node whose <code>id</code> is the <em>principal\nverb</em>'s token id (the last, most specific component -- e.g. \"eating\"\nin \"was eating\", \"eaten\" in \"was being eaten\") and whose <code>value</code> is\nevery component auxiliary/verb token's text joined by spaces in\nsurface order (e.g. \"was eating\"). An adverb that happens to\ninterrupt the auxiliary chain (e.g. \"not\", \"yet\" in \"was not yet\nbeing eaten\") is NOT a component token -- it is excluded from\n<code>value</code>, which is still just \"was being eaten\". An <em>independent</em>\naction (not embedded in another clause) has related_node=None; a\n<em>dependent</em> (subordinate) action has related_node set to the id of\nthe action node for the clause that governs it.</p>\n\n<p>For every action, also extract:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>its <em>agent</em>: the subject of an active-voice, intransitive, or\nlinking verb, or the by-phrase agent of a passive-voice verb.\nrelated_node = that action's id.</li>\n<li>its <em>target</em>: the direct object of a transitive active-voice\n  verb, the predicate of a linking verb, or the subject of a\n  transitive passive-voice verb. related_node = that action's id.\nEither may be absent if the passage doesn't express one (e.g. an\nintransitive verb has no target; an agentless passive has no\nagent; a verb taking a clausal complement rather than a noun-phrase\ndirect object -- e.g. \"said\" in \"He said that...\") has no target).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Every node's <code>id</code> must be the id of an existing token from the input\n<code>tokens</code> list (the principal verb's id, for a compound action) --\nnever a new id not present in <code>tokens</code>. Every node's <code>context</code> must\nmatch the context shared by every token in <code>tokens</code>.</p>\n\n<p>Worked examples from aat-model.md:</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li>\"The dog ate my homework.\" -> action node id=<id of \"ate\">,\nvalue=\"ate\", related_node=None; agent node id=<id of \"dog\">,\nvalue=\"dog\", related_node=<the action's id>; target node id=<id\nof \"homework\">, value=\"homework\", related_node=<the action's id>.</li>\n<li>\"The homework was eaten by the dog.\" (passive) -> action node\nanchored on \"eaten\" (value \"was eaten\"); agent node on \"dog\"\n(the by-phrase agent); target node on \"homework\" (the passive\nsubject).</li>\n<li>\"The homework was not yet being eaten.\" (compound, passive,\nno agent expressed) -> one action node, id=<id of \"eaten\">,\nvalue=\"was being eaten\" (the adverbs \"not\"/\"yet\" are excluded),\nrelated_node=None; target node on \"homework\"; no agent node.</li>\n<li>\"He said that the dog ate his homework.\" (independent + dependent\nclause) -> action node on \"said\" (related_node=None, no target\nsince it takes a clausal complement) with its own agent (\"He\");\naction node on \"ate\" with related_node=&lt;\"said\"'s id>, with its\nown agent (\"dog\") and target (\"homework\").</li>\n</ul>\n", "bases": "dspy.signatures.signature.Signature"}, "aat.english.AgentActionTarget.passage": {"fullname": "aat.english.AgentActionTarget.passage", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "AgentActionTarget.passage", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>The English passage's raw text.</p>\n", "annotation": ": str", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.english.AgentActionTarget.tokens": {"fullname": "aat.english.AgentActionTarget.tokens", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "AgentActionTarget.tokens", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>This passage's pre-tokenized CitableToken list, in reading order.</p>\n", "annotation": ": List[aat.core.tokens.CitableToken]", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.english.AgentActionTarget.nodes": {"fullname": "aat.english.AgentActionTarget.nodes", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "AgentActionTarget.nodes", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p>Every agent/action/target node this passage yields, per the AAT model.</p>\n", "annotation": ": List[aat.core.graph.AATNode]", "default_value": "PydanticUndefined"}, "aat.english.analyze": {"fullname": "aat.english.analyze", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "analyze", "kind": "variable", "doc": "<p></p>\n", "default_value": "predict = Predict(StringSignature(passage, tokens -&gt; reasoning, nodes\n    instructions=&#x27;Analyze an English passage according to the Agent-Action-Target\\n(AAT) model documented in aat-model.md.\\n\\nExtract every *action* (verbal expression): a single token for a\\nsimple verb (e.g. &quot;ate&quot;), or, for a compound verbal expression (e.g.\\n&quot;was eating&quot;, &quot;was being eaten&quot;), a node whose `id` is the *principal\\nverb*\\&#x27;s token id (the last, most specific component -- e.g. &quot;eating&quot;\\nin &quot;was eating&quot;, &quot;eaten&quot; in &quot;was being eaten&quot;) and whose `value` is\\nevery component auxiliary/verb token\\&#x27;s text joined by spaces in\\nsurface order (e.g. &quot;was eating&quot;). An adverb that happens to\\ninterrupt the auxiliary chain (e.g. &quot;not&quot;, &quot;yet&quot; in &quot;was not yet\\nbeing eaten&quot;) is NOT a component token -- it is excluded from\\n`value`, which is still just &quot;was being eaten&quot;. An *independent*\\naction (not embedded in another clause) has related_node=None; a\\n*dependent* (subordinate) action has related_node set to the id of\\nthe action node for the clause that governs it.\\n\\nFor every action, also extract:\\n  - its *agent*: the subject of an active-voice, intransitive, or\\n    linking verb, or the by-phrase agent of a passive-voice verb.\\n    related_node = that action\\&#x27;s id.\\n  - its *target*: the direct object of a transitive active-voice\\n    verb, the predicate of a linking verb, or the subject of a\\n    transitive passive-voice verb. related_node = that action\\&#x27;s id.\\n  Either may be absent if the passage doesn\\&#x27;t express one (e.g. an\\n  intransitive verb has no target; an agentless passive has no\\n  agent; a verb taking a clausal complement rather than a noun-phrase\\n  direct object -- e.g. &quot;said&quot; in &quot;He said that...&quot;) has no target).\\n\\nEvery node\\&#x27;s `id` must be the id of an existing token from the input\\n`tokens` list (the principal verb\\&#x27;s id, for a compound action) --\\nnever a new id not present in `tokens`. Every node\\&#x27;s `context` must\\nmatch the context shared by every token in `tokens`.\\n\\nWorked examples from aat-model.md:\\n  - &quot;The dog ate my homework.&quot; -&gt; action node id=&lt;id of &quot;ate&quot;&gt;,\\n    value=&quot;ate&quot;, related_node=None; agent node id=&lt;id of &quot;dog&quot;&gt;,\\n    value=&quot;dog&quot;, related_node=&lt;the action\\&#x27;s id&gt;; target node id=&lt;id\\n    of &quot;homework&quot;&gt;, value=&quot;homework&quot;, related_node=&lt;the action\\&#x27;s id&gt;.\\n  - &quot;The homework was eaten by the dog.&quot; (passive) -&gt; action node\\n    anchored on &quot;eaten&quot; (value &quot;was eaten&quot;); agent node on &quot;dog&quot;\\n    (the by-phrase agent); target node on &quot;homework&quot; (the passive\\n    subject).\\n  - &quot;The homework was not yet being eaten.&quot; (compound, passive,\\n    no agent expressed) -&gt; one action node, id=&lt;id of &quot;eaten&quot;&gt;,\\n    value=&quot;was being eaten&quot; (the adverbs &quot;not&quot;/&quot;yet&quot; are excluded),\\n    related_node=None; target node on &quot;homework&quot;; no agent node.\\n  - &quot;He said that the dog ate his homework.&quot; (independent + dependent\\n    clause) -&gt; action node on &quot;said&quot; (related_node=None, no target\\n    since it takes a clausal complement) with its own agent (&quot;He&quot;);\\n    action node on &quot;ate&quot; with related_node=&lt;&quot;said&quot;\\&#x27;s id&gt;, with its\\n    own agent (&quot;dog&quot;) and target (&quot;homework&quot;).&#x27;\n    passage = Field(annotation=str required=True description=&quot;The English passage&#x27;s raw text.&quot; json_schema_extra={&#x27;__dspy_field_type&#x27;: &#x27;input&#x27;, &#x27;desc&#x27;: &quot;The English passage&#x27;s raw text.&quot;, &#x27;prefix&#x27;: &#x27;Passage:&#x27;})\n    tokens = Field(annotation=List[CitableToken] required=True description=&quot;This passage&#x27;s pre-tokenized CitableToken list, in reading order.&quot; json_schema_extra={&#x27;__dspy_field_type&#x27;: &#x27;input&#x27;, &#x27;desc&#x27;: &quot;This passage&#x27;s pre-tokenized CitableToken list, in reading order.&quot;, &#x27;prefix&#x27;: &#x27;Tokens:&#x27;})\n    reasoning = Field(annotation=str required=True json_schema_extra={&#x27;desc&#x27;: &#x27;${reasoning}&#x27;, &#x27;__dspy_field_type&#x27;: &#x27;output&#x27;, &#x27;prefix&#x27;: &#x27;Reasoning:&#x27;})\n    nodes = Field(annotation=List[AATNode] required=True description=&#x27;Every agent/action/target node this passage yields, per the AAT model.&#x27; json_schema_extra={&#x27;__dspy_field_type&#x27;: &#x27;output&#x27;, &#x27;desc&#x27;: &#x27;Every agent/action/target node this passage yields, per the AAT model.&#x27;, &#x27;prefix&#x27;: &#x27;Nodes:&#x27;})\n))"}, "aat.english.validate": {"fullname": "aat.english.validate", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "validate", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Validate an <code>analyze()</code> prediction's <code>nodes</code> against its input\n<code>tokens</code> -- a thin wrapper around aat.core.validate.validate, so\ncallers working only with aat.english don't need their own separate\nimport from aat.core just for this.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitableToken</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">prediction</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">dspy</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">primitives</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prediction</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prediction</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">str</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.english.analyze_passage": {"fullname": "aat.english.analyze_passage", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "analyze_passage", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Convenience wrapper for the common case of a single string rather\nthan a list of CitedPassage. Wraps <code>text</code> as one CitedPassage (using\n<code>context</code> if given, else an empty string) and runs it through\nanalyze_passages().</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">text</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"s1\">''</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitableToken</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.english.analyze_passages": {"fullname": "aat.english.analyze_passages", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "analyze_passages", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Tokenize and analyze every passage in <code>passages</code>, independently\n(each passage's tokens are numbered from 't1' within its own context\n-- see CitableToken's docstring), and return (tokens, graph): <code>tokens</code>\nis every passage's tokens concatenated in order, <code>graph</code> is one\nAATGraph combining every passage's nodes.</p>\n\n<p>Prints a warning for any passage whose analysis fails validate() (a\nreferential problem -- see aat.core.validate.validate); it does not\nraise, since a referential problem is a sign the LM's output needs a\nre-run or a prompt tweak, not necessarily that the caller's own code\nis broken.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">passages</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitedPassage</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">Tuple</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitableToken</span><span class=\"p\">],</span> <span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">graph</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">AATGraph</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.english.aat_metric": {"fullname": "aat.english.aat_metric", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "aat_metric", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Score a prediction's <code>nodes</code> against <code>gold.nodes</code> (both lists of\nAATNode). Returns dspy.Prediction(score=..., feedback=...) -- GEPA's\nexpected \"ScoreWithFeedback\" shape. <code>pred_name</code>/<code>pred_trace</code> are\naccepted for protocol compatibility (GEPA can call a metric either at\nthe program level or per-predictor level) but not used to change\nscoring -- there's only one predictor in <code>analyze</code>.</p>\n\n<p><code>score</code> is in [0, 1]: the fraction of (gold-node-count +\nextra-predicted-node-count) correctly accounted for, where a gold\nnode counts as correct only if the prediction has a node at the same\n(context, id, role) with a matching <code>value</code> and <code>related_node</code>.\n<code>feedback</code> names every missing, extra, or mismatched node.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">gold</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">dspy</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">primitives</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">example</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Example</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">pred</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">dspy</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">primitives</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prediction</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prediction</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">trace</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">object</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">pred_name</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">str</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">pred_trace</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">object</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span>,</span><span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">program_trace</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"nb\">object</span> <span class=\"o\">|</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span></span><span class=\"return-annotation\">) -> <span class=\"n\">dspy</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">primitives</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">prediction</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prediction</span>:</span></span>", "funcdef": "def"}, "aat.english.tokens_to_html": {"fullname": "aat.english.tokens_to_html", "modulename": "aat.english", "qualname": "tokens_to_html", "kind": "function", "doc": "<p>Render <code>tokens</code> as one continuous HTML string: ordinary words get\na space before them, punctuation attaches per this module's own\ndocstring (left-joining by default; opening brackets and the first\nof a quote pair right-join instead).</p>\n\n<p>If <code>graph</code> is given, every token whose (context, id) matches a node\nin <code>graph</code> is highlighted: background/text colored the same way\nthat node is colored in <code>aat.core.mermaid.graph_to_mermaid()</code>'s\ndiagram (via <code>aat.core.coloring.assign_action_colors()</code>), with a\nrole-specific border -- a box around an <code>action</code> token, a rounded\nbox around an <code>agent</code> token, an underline under a <code>target</code> token.\nOmit <code>graph</code> (or pass <code>None</code>) for plain, unhighlighted text.</p>\n\n<p>Every token's text is HTML-escaped before being emitted, span or\nnot -- real passage text can contain a literal <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, <code>&amp;</code>, or\nquote character, which would otherwise be indistinguishable from\nmarkup to anything that re-parses this output.</p>\n", "signature": "<span class=\"signature pdoc-code multiline\">(<span class=\"param\">\t<span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"n\">aat</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">core</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tokens</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">CitableToken</span><span clas